{"step_index":390,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-04T06:02:09Z","input_tokens":2604,"cache_read_tokens":144359,"output_tokens":1490,"thinking":"Examining the logs for `PID_4EE7`, `PID_0D02`, and `VID_1B8E` reveals differences in how fastboot is handled across processes. Lines 3150-3172 of the `SESION_FASTBOOT_B866V2.log` file are being reviewed again to identify potential issues or discrepancies in fastboot detection. The goal is to understand how fastboot is detected and exited.\n\n\nThe initial attempt to unlock `/dev/block/env` failed because the device is locked, prompting a switch to U-Boot Fastboot. Subsequent steps successfully queried the unlock ability and then unlocked the device. Critical unlocking was also successfully executed.\n\n\nThe `fastbootd` process rejects the flash command because U-Boot reported the device is locked. U-Boot reads the lock state from `/dev/block/env`, where the unlock ability is zero. This prevents unlocking via `fastboot flashing unlock`, causing subsequent operations like flashing `vbmeta` to fail due to the device remaining locked.\n\n\nThe device's unlock process remains unclear, especially how `/dev/block/env` is modified from a locked to unlocked state, absent physical intervention or specific user actions. Examining the UART log (`BLOQUES_ASCII_COMPLETOS_SESION.txt`), the sequence around line 4400 reveals an unexpected upgrade key detection and U-Boot commands related to integer comparisons, suggesting a potential software-based unlock mechanism. The presence of \"Unknown command 'wipeisb'\" raises further questions about how the unlock occurs.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"Select-String -Path \\\"c:\\\\Users\\\\andre\\\\OneDrive\\\\Desktop\\\\xview\\\\experimento\\\\*\\\\*\\\" -Pattern \\\"wipeisb|detect upgrade key|upgrade_key\\\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object -First 30\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Search for upgrade_key and wipeisb in experimento\""}}]}
